{#- Guidance Layer -#}
Please only generate the character roster anchor. Subsequent character profiles, relationship networks, and arcs will be based on this list, so do not write full profiles.

## Output Field Description
- `character_roster`: Character roster list, each entry containing `name` (canonical full name), `role` (protagonist/antagonist/deuteragonist/supporting/minor), `age`, `gender`, `status` (active/dormant/retired), `time_layer` (modern/past/cross_temporal/memory_only/default), `function` (brief functional description).

## Chain Boundary
This template is only for the first step of the split character generation chain; it does not generate a complete CharacterBible.
This round's output is the sole roster anchor for subsequent profile_batch, relationship_matrix, and arc_plan.
Do not output `character_bible`, `character_profiles`, `relationship_matrix`, or `character_arcs`.
If `character_generation_mode` appears in context, use it only to confirm the current chain; do not write it into character fields.

## Canonical Name Rules
- `name` is the canonical name in the character system; downstream chapter prompts, entity registry, relationship matrix, and canon will all use it.
- Old names, aliases, past-life names, misnames, titles, or stage identities cannot create separate characters; only explain their relationship to the canonical name in `function` with a short phrase.
- If one surface name may point to multiple entities, use parentheses to generate different canonical names; if they are different names for the same entity, keep only one roster entry.
- Do not preemptively expand characters to fill relationships or arcs; this phase only ensures roster stability and clear character functions.

